  "note": "ADR 0016 Shelf-B `lists` bundle v1.2.0 — completes the relational list library (issue #333). SUPERSET of lists@1.1.0: it RE-INCLUDES every 1.1.0 relation BYTE-IDENTICALLY (same clauses, same ClauseId::canonical — `append`, `length`, `member`, `reverse`/`rev_`, `nth0`/`nth0_`, `last`) and ADDS the two standard relations `nth1/3` (1-indexed access) and `select/3` (element extraction with the remainder). lists@1.1.0.json is UNCHANGED and stays byte-pinned by its own differential vector; 1.2.0 is a NEW, additive bundle (Shelf B is byte-frozen per name@version). The new relations are ordinary account `Rule` nodes the EXISTING check() verifies as §7 dual-conformance derivations — ZERO new trusted code, no account node kind. Each new relation is range-restricted, safe, and terminating: `nth1` is the 1-indexed sibling of `nth0`, counting from `int(1)` via the same is/2 accumulator over the FROZEN ontos/data §5.1 `int` embedding (`nth1(I,L,X):-nth1_(L,int(1),I,X). nth1_([H|_],I,I,H). nth1_([_|T],I0,I,X):-I1 is I0+int(1), nth1_(T,I1,I,X).`) so it is multi-directional (index→element AND enumerate-index); `select(X,[X|T],T). select(X,[H|T],[H|R]):-select(X,T,R).` is structure-only (resolves by unification alone, NO theory) and multi-directional (pick-an-element, or insert-an-element). `nth1` invokes the ArithmeticTheory's `is/2`; `select` invokes no theory. The int payloads here are int(1)=atom 0001 (sign byte 0x00 then big-endian minimal magnitude). `program_digest` = lowercase-hex SHA-256(PROGRAM_PREFIX 'logos/account/program/v1\\n' || concat of len-prefixed SORTED ontos-codec(quote(clause-as-term)) bytes), recomputed and verified by load_prelude. Each clause `id` = ClauseId::canonical. Term notation as in vectors/account.json: term = {atom:<hex>}|{atom_str:<utf8>}|{tuple:[...]}|{var:<id>}; goal = {pred:<utf8>, args:[term...]}; negated body literal = {neg:<goal>}.",
